        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/wrf.jl::WRFFileSet",
        "domain_id": "d01",
        "projection": "lambert_conformal_conic",
        "map_proj": 1,
        "lcc_parameters": {
          "truelat1": 30.0,
          "truelat2": 60.0,
          "cen_lat": 38.999996,
          "stand_lon": -97.0,
          "sphere_radius_m": 6370000.0
        },
        "native_resolution_m": {
          "west_east": 12000.0,
          "south_north": 12000.0
        },
        "native_extent_m": {
          "west_east": [
            -2334000.0,
            2334000.0
          ],
          "south_north": [
            -1374000.0,
            1374000.0
          ]
        },
        "mass_grid_dimensions": [
          389,
          229,
          32
        ],
        "model_version": "WRF-Chem v3.9.1",
        "proj4_string": "+proj=lcc +lat_1=30.0 +lat_2=60.0 +lat_0=38.999996 +lon_0=-97.0 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +a=6370000 +b=6370000 +to_meter=1",
        "wrf_variable_note": "The upstream WRF() constructor reads ALL variables in the WRF output file dynamically via WRFFileSet.varnames(). This loader documents the nine core meteorological variables (U, V, W, T, PH, PHB, P, PB, QVAPOR) present in all CONUS d340000 files and that drive EarthSciML coupling. Additional WRF-Chem tracer/diagnostic variables (T2, U10, V10, PSFC, chemistry species) can be added as additional loader variables.",
        "staggering_note": "WRF uses an Arakawa C-grid. Staggered-grid variables (U on west_east_stag, V on south_north_stag, W/PH/PHB on bottom_top_stag) live on the cell-edge dimensions; scalars (T, P, PB, QVAPOR) live on the mass (cell-centred) dimensions. The regridding model (wrf.esm) regrids the C-grid wind components U/V/W with a B-spline interpolating kernel and the scalars conservatively (RFC §5.2). The upstream EarthSciData.jl loader de-staggers staggered variables to cell centres in loadmetadata; the GDD grid above preserves the native staggered dimensions so the regridding model can choose the kernel by location.",
        "access_note": "UCAR RDA data access requires a free registration at https://rda.ucar.edu/. The upstream EarthSciData.jl WRFFileSet uses standard HTTP downloads (login cookie only). Ensure $EARTHSCIDATADIR is set for local caching.",
        "w_extrapolation_note": "Vertical wind W uses zero-boundary extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0) in the upstream loader to prevent spurious mass transport through the ground surface. All other variables use clamp extrapolation. Per-variable extrapolation override is a future ESM-schema concern; here it is documented for the runtime."
      }
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WRF": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.1). The pre-migration wrf.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.WRF_hourly_d01 block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader is now the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/wrf_loader.esm, referenced here as subsystem `raw`.\n\nUpstream WRF(domaininfo; name=:WRF, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon/lat (rad) when pvars include :lat/:lon, or x/y (m) when pvars include :x/:y; lev (1); t_ref (s)\n  - For every varname in WRFFileSet.varnames(fs), one DataSetInterpolator and one observed equation via create_interp_equation (uses interp_unsafe). These are now provided by the loader subsystem `raw` (raw.<var>) and re-exposed as model observed variables U/V/W/T/PH/PHB/P/PB/QVAPOR for the coupling contract.\n  - Staggered grids: PH/PHB/W on bottom_top_stag (N+1 z-points), U on west_east_stag (N+1 x-points), V on south_north_stag (N+1 y-points); the upstream loader de-staggers to mass centres in loadmetadata. In the new pipeline the native staggered dimensions are preserved on the loader's GDD grid and the wind components are regridded with a B-spline kernel (RFC §5.2).\n  - Extrapolation: W uses extrapolate_type=0.0 (zero below ground); all others use Flat() (clamp).\n  - Derived observed variables: P_total ~ P + PB; z ~ (PH + PHB)/g with g=9.80665 m/s²; δxδlon ~ lon2m·cos(lat) and δyδlat ~ lat2meters (only when :lat in pvdict), lon2m = 40075e3/(2π) ≈ 6378134.3, lat2meters = 111.32e3·180/π ≈ 6378166.0.\n  - couple2 with MeanWindCoupler: maps WRF.U/V/W → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev via _couple_meanwind.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): WRF's native grid.crs.projection is 'lambert_conformal', so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm (esd-47z.2), parameterized by the loader crs parameters {lat_1:30, lat_2:60, lat_0:38.999996, lon_0:-97} on a sphere of radius R=6370000 m. The projected-grid construction (corner geometry via inverse LCC) is ESD discretizations/grids/lambert_conformal/wrf_lcc.esm (esd-47z.5).\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The Arakawa-C-grid wind components U (west_east_stag), V (south_north_stag), W (bottom_top_stag) are edge/face-staggered → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3). The cell-centered scalars T, PH, PHB, P, PB, QVAPOR → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm). (PH/PHB are geopotential scalars even though they reside on the staggered w-levels; they are mass-like quantities regridded conservatively.)\n\nδzδlev gap (gt-p3ep(lookup)): evaluating PH and PHB at lev+1 requires the indexed-offset form of loader evaluation (a gt-p3ep(lookup) expression) not yet representable in the ESM expression language. δzδlev is omitted from this migration. When gt-p3ep(lookup) is resolved, add δzδlev = (raw.PH@lev+1 + raw.PHB@lev+1 - raw.PH - raw.PHB)/9.80665.\n\nCoordinate system: this ESM targets the lat/lon coordinate form (pvars contain :lat and :lon). For LCC-projected (x/y) domains the loader uses pvars :x and :y; δxδlon/δyδlat are not emitted in that case.\n\nLive tests (informational; require UCAR RDA NetCDF files, not run in CI): EarthSciData.jl wrf_test.jl expected values at (lon=-118.2707°, lat=34.0059°):\n  P_total at lev=[1,1.5,2,21.5,30,31.5]: [100331.86, 100235.72, 100139.58, 67846.08, 30679.47, 28729.87] Pa\n  W at lev=[0.5,1,1.5,2,21.5,30,31.5]: [0.0, 5.205e-3, 1.041e-2, 1.164e-2, -1.698e-2, 2.697e-2, 2.244e-2] m/s\n\nCoupler identity: this model was serialized with the model-level field `coupletype: \"WRFCoupler\"`, the EarthSciMLBase `CoupleType` metadata tag naming the Julia coupler struct that `EarthSciMLBase.couple2` dispatches on to find this component's pairwise coupling rules. The esm schema defined `coupletype` only before 0.8.0 (\"informational label identifying this system's role in coupling\"); 0.8.0 removed it in favour of explicit coupling — `coupling` entries naming components directly, or `coupling_roles` + `coupling_import` in a coupling-library file (esm-spec §10.9–§10.11). esm 1.0.0 has no model-level coupler-identity field, so the tag is recorded here to keep it recoverable.\n\nRegridding intent: this model was serialized with the model-level `regrid` map, one entry per variable naming the kernel that transfers the loaded native-grid field onto the consuming model's grid. The esm schema defined `regrid` only before 0.8.0. esm 1.0.0 states (esm-spec §8.6) that a data source performs no regridding and that there is NO `Model.regrid` map: the carrier is the `variable_map` entry's `transform` field on the coupling edge that consumes the field (§10.4/§10.5) — an ordinary `aggregate` expression, typically an `apply_expression_template` invocation of an imported overlap-weight library. No such coupling edge exists in this document, so the per-variable kernel choice is recorded here verbatim to keep it recoverable. This is a demotion from a structured field to prose, not an equivalent — the transform expression still has to be authored on whichever coupling edge consumes these fields.\n\n  U: method bspline — Zonal wind on west_east_stag (Arakawa-C x-edges). Edge-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3).\n  V: method bspline — Meridional wind on south_north_stag (Arakawa-C y-edges). Edge-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (esd-47z.3).\n  W: method bspline — Vertical wind on bottom_top_stag (Arakawa-C z-edges). Face-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (esd-47z.3).\n  T: method conservative — Perturbation potential temperature (K). Cell-centered scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap-join regridder (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm).\n  PH: method conservative — Perturbation geopotential (m²/s²). A geopotential scalar (mass-like quantity, regridded conservatively even though it resides on the staggered w-levels).\n  PHB: method conservative — Base-state geopotential (m²/s²). A geopotential scalar → conservative regridder (see PH).\n  P: method conservative — Perturbation pressure (Pa). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder.\n  PB: method conservative — Base-state pressure (Pa). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder.\n  QVAPOR: method conservative — Water vapor mixing ratio (kg/kg). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. Used as the x-axis coordinate for WRF data interpolation in lat/lon domains."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. Used as the y-axis coordinate for WRF data interpolation in lat/lon domains."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Vertical level index (dimensionless, 1-based integer corresponding to the WRF bottom_top layer). Fractional values interpolate between layers. Coupled from the simulation domain's lev coordinate."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reference epoch (seconds since the Julian date epoch) from which the WRF file time axis is offset. Set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time."
        },
        "U": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Zonal (west–east) wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.U (WRF variable U on the west_east_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lon via WRFCoupler/couple2.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "U",
              "description": "Zonal (west–east) wind component. WRF output variable U on the west_east_stag grid (C-grid x-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel."
            }
          }
        },
        "V": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Meridional (south–north) wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.V (WRF variable V on the south_north_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lat via WRFCoupler/couple2.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "V",
              "description": "Meridional (south–north) wind component. WRF output variable V on the south_north_stag grid (C-grid y-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel."
            }
          }
        },
        "W": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Vertical wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.W (WRF variable W on the bottom_top_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Zero-extrapolated below the surface in the upstream loader. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lev via WRFCoupler/couple2.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "W",
              "description": "Vertical wind component. WRF output variable W on the bottom_top_stag grid (C-grid z-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel. Zero extrapolation below the surface (extrapolate_type=0.0 in the upstream loader, overriding the default clamp for this variable only)."
            }
          }
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Perturbation potential temperature (K). Full potential temperature θ = T + 300 K. Cell-centred (mass grid), conservatively regridded. Sourced from raw.T.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "T",
              "description": "Perturbation potential temperature (K). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Full potential temperature θ = T + 300 K."
            }
          }
        },
        "PH": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Perturbation geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. PH + PHB gives total geopotential. Sourced from raw.PH.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "PH",
              "description": "Perturbation geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. Together with PHB provides geopotential height z = (PH+PHB)/g."
            }
          }
        },
        "PHB": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Base-state geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. PH + PHB gives total geopotential. Sourced from raw.PHB.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "PHB",
              "description": "Base-state geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. Together with PH provides geopotential height z = (PH+PHB)/g."
            }
          }
        },
        "P": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Perturbation pressure (Pa). Cell-centred (mass grid). P + PB gives total atmospheric pressure. Sourced from raw.P.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "P",
              "description": "Perturbation pressure (Pa). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Together with PB provides total atmospheric pressure P_total = P + PB."
            }
          }
        },
        "PB": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Base-state pressure (Pa). Cell-centred (mass grid). P + PB gives total atmospheric pressure. Sourced from raw.PB.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "PB",
              "description": "Base-state pressure (Pa). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Together with P provides total atmospheric pressure P_total = P + PB."
            }
          }
        },
        "QVAPOR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Water vapor mixing ratio (kg water per kg dry air). Cell-centred (mass grid). Sourced from raw.QVAPOR.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "WRF_hourly_d01",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "QVAPOR",
              "description": "Water vapor mixing ratio (kg water kg⁻¹ dry air). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred."
            }
          }
        },
        "P_total": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Total atmospheric pressure (Pa): P_total = P + PB. Sum of perturbation and base-state pressure components, both on the mass grid. Computed from the loader fields raw.P and raw.PB."
        },
        "z": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Geopotential height (m): z = (PH + PHB) / g, where g = 9.80665 m s⁻². Computed from the w-level geopotential components. Corresponds to the upstream z ~ (PH_itp + PHB_itp) / g_const equation."
        },
        "δxδlon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: x-distance per unit longitude (m rad⁻¹). δxδlon = lon2m·cos(lat) where lon2m = 40075×10³/(2π) ≈ 6378134 m rad⁻¹ (equatorial circumference metric). Non-zero only in lat/lon coordinate domains; the upstream constructor emits this equation only when :lat is in DomainInfo.pvars."
        },
        "δyδlat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: y-distance per unit latitude (m rad⁻¹). δyδlat = lat2meters = 111.32×10³·(180/π) ≈ 6378166 m rad⁻¹. Constant (does not depend on position). Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "P_total",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "P",
              "PB"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "z",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "PH",
                  "PHB"
                ]
              },
              9.80665
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "δxδlon",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              6378134.3,
              {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  "lat"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "δyδlat",
          "rhs": 6378166.0
        }
      ],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
